.SH NAME
floor, fabs, ceil, fmod \- absolute value, floor, ceiling functions 
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fB#include <math.h>\fR
.PP
\fBdouble fabs\fR(\fIx\fR)
\fBdouble\fR(\fIx\fR);
.PP
\fBdouble floor\fR(\fIx\fR)
\fBdouble \fIx\fR;
.PP
\fBdouble ceil\fR(\fIx\fR)
\fBdouble \fIx\fR;
.PP
\fBdouble fmod\fR(\fIx\fR, \fIy\fR)
\fBdouble \fIx\fR, \fIy\fR;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Fabs
returns the absolute value
.RI | \|x\| |.
.PP
.B Floor
returns the
largest integer
not greater than
.IR x.
.PP
.B Ceil
returns the
smallest integer
not less than
.IR x.
.PP
.B Fmod
returns the number
.IR f
such that
\fIx = iy + f\fR,
for some integer,
.I i,
and
\fI0 <= f < y\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
abs(3).
